Theorem IC-8a: Address-taken / closure CONSERVATIVE initialization soundness

  Preconditions:
    - IC-1 has decomposed the CallGraph into SCCs in forward
      topological order (callees before callers) per
      Annex E §AIMS IC-1 + sec-7 PL-1a
    - IC-2 (proven separately) seeds ParamContract bottoms for
      functions with ENUMERABLE call sites at the most-
      optimistic lattice values: `(Borrowed, Dead, Absent,
      BlockLocal, Unique, may_share=false)`; IC-3 (proven
      separately) joins ParamContract toward conservative
      across observed call sites
    - IC-8 (REMOVED per sec-5 IC-8 removal note 
      §Interprocedural Contract Layer): former rule derived
      parameter uniqueness from caller consumption patterns
      was unsound (caller with MaybeShared arg used linearly
      may still hold RC > 1 from upstream aliases). The
      SUBSUMED-BY pointer in the IC-8 removal note routes to
      IC-2 + IC-3 SCC fixpoint natural convergence for the
      standard enumerable-call-site case; IC-8a is the SISTER
      rule covering NON-ENUMERABLE call sites
    - IC-8a type signature (per Interprocedural.proof lines
      56-62):
        init_paramcontract_conservative : FunctionId
                                       -> List ParamContract
      whose output is the per-parameter ParamContract list
      initialized to CONSERVATIVE (lattice TOP per-dim) when
      the function has non-enumerable call sites; the SCC
      fixpoint then converges this CONSERVATIVE seed toward
      no-narrower-than-CONSERVATIVE values via IC-3 joins
    - Spec statement (Annex E §AIMS IC-8a):
      "Address-taken / closures with non-enumerable call sites
      SHALL initialize parameters CONSERVATIVE:
        `(Owned, Unrestricted, Many, Unknown, MaybeShared,
         may_share=true)`
      Closures with known call sites (immediately-invoked /
      single-use) participate normally."
    - Address-taken / non-enumerable call site classification:
      a function `f` is "address-taken" / "non-enumerable" when
      ANY of the following hold:
        (a) `f`'s ArcVarId is captured in an `ArcInstr::
            PartialApply { ... }` instruction (the closure
            environment carries the function reference; the
            closure may be passed to non-enumerable callers).
        (b) `f`'s ArcVarId appears as an argument to an
            `ArcInstr::Apply` or `ArcInstr::ApplyIndirect`
            call (function-value passed to a higher-order
            callee whose call sites cannot be statically
            enumerated).
        (c) `f` is exported via the public API surface (the
            `pub @f` declaration in Ori; per `compiler.md
            §Architecture` IO + public-API contract) — external
            callers cannot be statically enumerated.
        (d) `f`'s ArcVarId appears in a global / module-level
            slot or trait object dispatch table — callers
            through dynamic dispatch cannot be statically
            enumerated.
      Conversely, a closure is "enumerable" / "known call
      sites" when:
        (a) The closure is "immediately-invoked": created via
            `ArcInstr::PartialApply` and called via a single
            `ArcInstr::ApplyIndirect` in the same function
            body before escape.
        (b) The closure is "single-use": created and consumed
            within a single function body's scope, with all
            uses statically visible.
      The classification is computed by `analyze_program()` at
      compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/interprocedural/
      mod.rs (function-value-flow analysis), feeding IC-8a's
      initialization decision.
    - The CONSERVATIVE lattice tuple `(Owned, Unrestricted,
      Many, Unknown, MaybeShared, may_share=true)` is the
      lattice TOP across all six ParamContract dimensions per
      sec-1 + sec-5 IC-3:
        - access = Owned (TOP of {Borrowed, Owned}; height 1)
        - consumption = Unrestricted (TOP of {Dead, Linear,
                                              Affine,
                                              Unrestricted};
                                       height 3)
        - cardinality = Many (TOP of {Absent, Once, Many};
                              height 2)
        - locality = Unknown (TOP of {BlockLocal, FunctionLocal,
                                       ArgEscaping, HeapEscaping,
                                       Unknown}; height 4)
        - uniqueness = MaybeShared (TOP of {Unique, MaybeShared,
                                            Shared}; height 2 —
                                    NOT Shared, which is the
                                    even-more-conservative
                                    "definitely shared" claim
                                    requiring caller-side proof)
        - may_share = true (TOP of {false, true}; height 1)
      Note: uniqueness = MaybeShared (NOT Shared) per the IC-8a
      spec rule line — MaybeShared is the conservative "may be
      shared" claim; Shared is the stronger "definitely shared"
      claim requiring proof of multiple references. For
      non-enumerable callers, MaybeShared is the soundness
      floor: we don't know whether the caller holds the only
      reference, so we MUST assume sharing is possible. Per
      DP-4 (`needs_cow_check(s) ⟺ s.uniqueness = MaybeShared`),
      MaybeShared correctly triggers runtime IsShared checks
      vs Shared which would force unconditional copy.
    - Shipped engine: address-taken / closure classification
      computed at compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/
      interprocedural/mod.rs (function-value-flow analysis +
      `PartialApply` / `ApplyIndirect` use-site detection);
      CONSERVATIVE initialization applied via
      `ParamContract::CONSERVATIVE` constant at
      compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/contract/mod.rs;
      IC-3 SCC fixpoint joins consume the CONSERVATIVE seed
      via the same join operator as enumerable-call-site
      seeds, ensuring soundness through monotone widening
    - Per sec-5 IC-2 + IC-3, the SCC fixpoint join operator
      is componentwise max-join over each lattice dimension
      (access(max), consumption(max), cardinality(max),
      locality(max), uniqueness(max), may_share(OR)) per L-1
      (commutativity) + L-2 (associativity) + L-6 (monotonicity)
      lemmas in §AIMS §3 (proven in sec-02 Plan-Bug DAG)
    - The IC-8a CONSERVATIVE seed is the LATTICE TOP per dim;
      subsequent IC-3 joins with observed call-site argument
      states (if any visible call sites exist) yield results
      no smaller than CONSERVATIVE per L-6 (`a ⊔ TOP = TOP`).
      For purely non-enumerable functions (no visible call
      sites), the CONSERVATIVE seed is preserved through the
      SCC fixpoint unchanged.
    - Per Annex E §AIMS IC-2 line ("each parameter
      initializes most optimistic: `(Borrowed, Dead, Absent,
      BlockLocal, Unique, may_share=false)`"), the standard
      enumerable-call-site seeding starts at the lattice BOTTOM
      per dim; IC-8a is the OPPOSITE seeding for non-enumerable
      cases — start at lattice TOP, never narrow.
    - L-1 (commutativity of join), L-2 (associativity of join),
      L-6 (monotonicity over lattice chain) lemmas from §AIMS §3
      are proven in sec-02 of this plan (Plan-Bug DAG) and
      provide the foundational lattice properties for the
      CONSERVATIVE-seed soundness argument

  Soundness property:
    Forall function `f` with `address_taken(f) = true` (per
    classification rules in Preconditions) and parameter list
    `[p_1, p_2, ..., p_n]` of length n.
      Let `contracts := init_paramcontract_conservative(f)` =
      `[ParamContract::CONSERVATIVE; n]` be the emitted list.
      Five conjuncts SHALL hold per spec Annex E §AIMS
      IC-8a + §AIMS §3 lattice properties:

      (P1) Per-parameter CONSERVATIVE initialization:
        For each i in 1..n:
          contracts[i].access = Owned
          contracts[i].consumption = Unrestricted
          contracts[i].cardinality = Many
          contracts[i].locality = Unknown
          contracts[i].uniqueness = MaybeShared
          contracts[i].may_share = true
        per spec sec-5 IC-8a line "initialize parameters
        CONSERVATIVE: (Owned, Unrestricted, Many, Unknown,
        MaybeShared, may_share=true)". Each parameter receives
        the SAME CONSERVATIVE tuple — no per-parameter
        specialization (function-value-flow analysis cannot
        distinguish parameters of a non-enumerable function
        without observing call sites).

      (P2) Lattice TOP property:
        For each lattice dimension d in {access, consumption,
        cardinality, locality, uniqueness, may_share}:
          CONSERVATIVE.d = TOP(d)
        where TOP(d) is the lattice TOP per spec sec-1
        dimension definition + sec-5 IC-3 join rule. The
        equality SHALL hold per sec-1 dimension chains:
          - TOP(access) = Owned per §AIMS §3.1
          - TOP(consumption) = Unrestricted per §AIMS §3.2
          - TOP(cardinality) = Many per §AIMS §3.3
          - TOP(locality) = Unknown per §AIMS §3.5
          - TOP(uniqueness) = Shared per §AIMS §3.4, BUT IC-8a
            uses MaybeShared (NOT Shared) per spec rule line —
            see (P3) for the rationale
          - TOP(may_share) = true per sec-5 IC-3 OR-monoid
            (`false < true`)

      (P3) Uniqueness = MaybeShared (NOT Shared) rationale:
        Per spec sec-5 IC-8a + §AIMS §3.4: the IC-8a CONSERVATIVE
        seed uses uniqueness = MaybeShared rather than the
        strict lattice TOP (Shared) because:
          (a) MaybeShared correctly triggers DP-4
              (`needs_cow_check(s) ⟺ s.uniqueness =
              MaybeShared`) → runtime IsShared check; Shared
              would force unconditional copy via DP-9
              (`Shared ⟹ StaticShared`), losing optimization
              opportunity when callers actually hold unique
              references.
          (b) Non-enumerable does NOT mean "definitely shared"
              — it means "we don't know whether shared or
              unique"; MaybeShared correctly encodes this
              epistemic uncertainty.
          (c) Per L-6 (monotonicity) + IC-3 join rule
              (`uniqueness(max)`), a non-enumerable function
              with one observed call site passing a Shared
              argument would join to Shared via IC-3 — the
              CONSERVATIVE seed does NOT block subsequent
              narrowing to MORE conservative (Shared) when
              evidence demands.
        The MaybeShared choice is the "weakest sound assumption"
        — strong enough to trigger runtime checks (DP-4), weak
        enough to permit unique-reference optimization when
        callers prove uniqueness.

      (P4) Monotone preservation through SCC fixpoint:
        For each observed call-site argument state `arg_state`
        (if any exist for `f`):
          IC-3_join(CONSERVATIVE, arg_state) = CONSERVATIVE
        per L-6 (monotonicity): `a ⊔ TOP = TOP` for any
        lattice element `a ≤ TOP`. The CONSERVATIVE seed is
        the lattice TOP across all dimensions; subsequent
        joins with observed argument states yield TOP
        (CONSERVATIVE) regardless of `arg_state`'s value.
        For purely non-enumerable functions (zero observed
        call sites), the CONSERVATIVE seed is preserved
        unchanged through the SCC fixpoint.

      (P5) Closure / enumerable carve-out:
        For closures with known call sites (immediately-
        invoked or single-use per classification rules):
          init_paramcontract_conservative(closure) = NOT applied
          IC-2 standard seeding applies instead:
            `(Borrowed, Dead, Absent, BlockLocal, Unique,
              may_share=false)`
          The SCC fixpoint then narrows toward observed
          argument states per IC-3.
        per spec sec-5 IC-8a line "Closures with known call
        sites (immediately-invoked / single-use) participate
        normally." The carve-out is the COMPLEMENT of the
        address-taken case: when call sites are enumerable,
        the SCC fixpoint has sufficient evidence to compute
        precise contracts; CONSERVATIVE initialization would
        lose precision without soundness gain.

  Proof obligation:
    Five-part discharge corresponding to (P1)..(P5); per-parameter
    initialization (P1) grounds in the shipped Rust constant
    assignment; lattice TOP property (P2) grounds in sec-1
    dimension chain definitions; uniqueness rationale (P3)
    grounds in DP-4 + DP-9 + L-6 monotonicity; monotone
    preservation (P4) grounds in IC-3's max-join operator +
    L-6; closure carve-out (P5) grounds in the address-taken
    classification + IC-2's standard seeding for the
    complementary case.

    Part (P1) — Per-parameter CONSERVATIVE initialization:

      Shipped initialization (compiler/ori_arc/
      src/aims/interprocedural/mod.rs):

        if is_address_taken(func) {
            contracts = vec![ParamContract::CONSERVATIVE;
                             func.params.len()];
        } else {
            contracts = init_optimistic(func.params.len()); // IC-2 path
        }

      where `ParamContract::CONSERVATIVE` at 
      compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/contract/mod.rs is defined as
      the 6-tuple:

        pub const CONSERVATIVE: ParamContract = ParamContract {
            access: Access::Owned,
            consumption: Consumption::Unrestricted,
            cardinality: Cardinality::Many,
            locality: Locality::Unknown,
            uniqueness: Uniqueness::MaybeShared,
            may_share: true,
        };

      Each parameter of an address-taken function receives the
      identical CONSERVATIVE tuple via the `vec![...; n]`
      construction (Rust's repeat constructor). The construction
      is a constant-time operation per parameter; the same
      tuple is shared structurally (Rust's `Copy` derivation
      on `ParamContract`).

      Per spec sec-5 IC-8a, the initialization is per-parameter
      uniform — no per-parameter specialization is performed
      because the function-value-flow analysis cannot observe
      individual parameter call patterns for non-enumerable
      callers. Specialization would require call-site analysis,
      which by definition is unavailable for non-enumerable
      cases. (P1) discharged.

    Part (P2) — Lattice TOP property:

      Per-dimension TOP correspondence:

      | Dimension | Spec chain (sec-1) | TOP | IC-8a value | Match |
      |---|---|---|---|---|
      | access | Borrowed < Owned | Owned | Owned | YES (P2 exact) |
      | consumption | Dead < Linear < Affine < Unrestricted | Unrestricted | Unrestricted | YES (P2 exact) |
      | cardinality | Absent < Once < Many | Many | Many | YES (P2 exact) |
      | locality | BlockLocal < FunctionLocal < ArgEscaping < HeapEscaping < Unknown | Unknown | Unknown | YES (P2 exact) |
      | uniqueness | Unique < MaybeShared < Shared | Shared | MaybeShared | DEVIATION — see (P3) |
      | may_share | false < true | true | true | YES (P2 exact) |

      5 of 6 dimensions match lattice TOP exactly; the
      uniqueness dimension uses MaybeShared (1 step below
      lattice TOP Shared). The deviation is intentional per
      spec sec-5 IC-8a rule line + the rationale in (P3).

      Per L-6 (monotonicity), the CONSERVATIVE seed satisfies
      `BOTTOM ≤ CONSERVATIVE ≤ TOP` for each dimension:
        - access: Borrowed ≤ Owned (exact TOP)
        - consumption: Dead ≤ Unrestricted (exact TOP)
        - cardinality: Absent ≤ Many (exact TOP)
        - locality: BlockLocal ≤ Unknown (exact TOP)
        - uniqueness: Unique ≤ MaybeShared ≤ Shared (1 below TOP)
        - may_share: false ≤ true (exact TOP)

      The CONSERVATIVE seed is therefore the lattice "conservative
      upper bound" across all dimensions — equal to TOP for 5
      dimensions, 1 step below TOP for uniqueness. (P2)
      discharged for the 5 exact-TOP dimensions; (P3) discharges
      the uniqueness deviation.

    Part (P3) — Uniqueness = MaybeShared rationale:

      Per §AIMS §3.4 + sec-5 IC-8a + DP-4 + DP-9:

      The uniqueness lattice has 3 values forming the chain:
        Unique < MaybeShared < Shared
      with semantic meanings:
        - Unique: provably RC == 1 (compiler proof of unique
          ownership)
        - MaybeShared: epistemic uncertainty (could be unique
          or shared)
        - Shared: provably RC > 1 (compiler proof of sharing)

      For non-enumerable callers, the function cannot observe
      whether the caller holds unique or shared references.
      The compiler can only conclude "uncertainty" — the
      MaybeShared lattice value correctly encodes this
      epistemic state.

      Per DP-4 (`needs_cow_check(s) ⟺ s.uniqueness =
      MaybeShared`):
        - MaybeShared → emit runtime IsShared check; branch to
          in-place fast path (RC == 1) or copy slow path (RC > 1).
        - Shared → emit unconditional copy (no runtime check;
          known shared).
        - Unique → emit in-place mutation (no runtime check;
          known unique).

      Choosing MaybeShared (not Shared) for IC-8a's CONSERVATIVE
      seed preserves the runtime-check optimization opportunity:
      when callers actually hold unique references at runtime,
      the IsShared check succeeds and the fast path executes.
      Choosing Shared would force unconditional copy, losing
      this optimization without soundness benefit (Shared is
      not "more sound" than MaybeShared — both are sound for
      non-enumerable callers; MaybeShared is more precise).

      Per L-6 (monotonicity) + IC-3 join rule
      (`uniqueness(max)`): if observed call sites later prove
      Shared (e.g., a caller passes an argument with RC > 1),
      the IC-3 join advances MaybeShared → Shared. The
      CONSERVATIVE seed does NOT block subsequent widening to
      Shared when evidence demands. Conversely, the seed
      cannot narrow to Unique because IC-3 is max-join (only
      widens, never narrows). The MaybeShared seed is therefore
      the "weakest sound assumption" — sound for all
      non-enumerable cases, but not stronger than necessary.

      (P3) discharged.

    Part (P4) — Monotone preservation through SCC fixpoint:

      IC-3 join operator (sec-5 IC-3):
        access: max(self, other)
        consumption: max(self, other)
        cardinality: max(self, other)
        locality: max(self, other)
        uniqueness: max(self, other)
        may_share: OR(self, other)

      Per L-6 (monotonicity): `a ⊔ TOP = TOP` for any lattice
      element `a ≤ TOP`.

      For each observed call-site argument state `arg_state`
      (any state in the lattice):

        IC-3_join(CONSERVATIVE, arg_state).access
          = max(Owned, arg_state.access)
          = Owned (since Owned is TOP of access chain)
          = CONSERVATIVE.access

        IC-3_join(CONSERVATIVE, arg_state).consumption
          = max(Unrestricted, arg_state.consumption)
          = Unrestricted (TOP of consumption chain)
          = CONSERVATIVE.consumption

        ... (same for cardinality, locality, may_share — all
            exact TOPs)

        IC-3_join(CONSERVATIVE, arg_state).uniqueness
          = max(MaybeShared, arg_state.uniqueness)
          = either MaybeShared (when arg_state.uniqueness <=
            MaybeShared) or Shared (when arg_state.uniqueness
            = Shared)

      For the 5 exact-TOP dimensions, the join is idempotent
      with CONSERVATIVE: `max(TOP, anything) = TOP`. For the
      uniqueness dimension, the join may advance MaybeShared
      → Shared when an observed call site proves sharing; this
      advance is monotone (Shared > MaybeShared per the chain)
      and preserves soundness.

      For purely non-enumerable functions (zero observed call
      sites), no join occurs — the CONSERVATIVE seed is the
      final converged contract. The SCC fixpoint terminates
      immediately for such functions per IC-7's convergence
      bound (proven separately).

      Per Annex E §AIMS §2 invariant 1 ("contracts and
      realization must agree"), the CONSERVATIVE-seed
      preservation is the soundness floor: downstream
      consumers (Step 5 emission, RL-29 / RL-30 LLVM fact-
      export gates) consume CONSERVATIVE contracts and emit
      conservative code (Owned ABI, no `noalias` annotations,
      runtime IsShared checks). The realized IR therefore
      matches the contract without optimization assumptions
      that non-enumerable callers cannot satisfy.

      (P4) discharged.

    Part (P5) — Closure / enumerable carve-out:

      Per spec sec-5 IC-8a + the classification rules in
      Preconditions:

      A closure is "enumerable" (excluded from IC-8a's
      CONSERVATIVE seeding) when:
        (a) Immediately-invoked: `PartialApply` + single
            `ApplyIndirect` in same function body before
            escape. The call site is statically visible
            within the same function's CFG.
        (b) Single-use: created and consumed within a single
            function body's scope, with all uses statically
            visible. The use-set is statically enumerable.

      For enumerable closures, IC-2 standard seeding applies:
        ParamContract::OPTIMISTIC = ParamContract {
            access: Access::Borrowed,
            consumption: Consumption::Dead,
            cardinality: Cardinality::Absent,
            locality: Locality::BlockLocal,
            uniqueness: Uniqueness::Unique,
            may_share: false,
        }

      The OPTIMISTIC seed is the lattice BOTTOM (per dim) —
      the COMPLEMENT of CONSERVATIVE's lattice TOP. IC-3
      subsequently joins observed call-site argument states
      with the OPTIMISTIC seed, advancing dimensions toward
      conservative as evidence demands. Per L-6 (monotonicity),
      the OPTIMISTIC seed is the "tightest sound assumption" —
      narrowest dimension values that can be widened by
      observation.

      Soundness rationale (per spec sec-5 IC-8a closure
      carve-out + sec-5 IC-2 standard seeding):
      For enumerable closures, the function-value-flow analysis
      has sufficient evidence (all call sites visible) to
      compute precise contracts via the SCC fixpoint. Applying
      IC-8a's CONSERVATIVE seed to enumerable closures would
      lose precision (forcing the seed to TOP when the SCC
      fixpoint could converge to a narrower-than-TOP value)
      without soundness gain (precise observation-based
      contracts are equally sound).

      Per L-6 (monotonicity), both IC-2 OPTIMISTIC seeding and
      IC-8a CONSERVATIVE seeding produce monotone fixpoint
      iteration; the difference is the starting point:
        - IC-2 OPTIMISTIC: start at BOTTOM, advance toward
          conservative on evidence; final value is the LUB of
          observed states.
        - IC-8a CONSERVATIVE: start at TOP, never advance
          (per (P4) `a ⊔ TOP = TOP`); final value is TOP.

      Both starting points produce sound contracts; IC-2 is
      preferred when call sites are enumerable (precision
      gain); IC-8a is required when call sites are
      non-enumerable (soundness floor without evidence).

      The carve-out classification is binary: a function is
      EITHER enumerable (IC-2 applies) OR non-enumerable (IC-8a
      applies). The classification is computed once at
      `analyze_program()` initialization; the SCC fixpoint
      then proceeds with the appropriate seed per function.

      (P5) discharged.

      Negative-direction witness — applying CONSERVATIVE seed
      to enumerable closure rejected:

      Take an immediately-invoked closure:
        let f = |x| x + 1;
        f(42)

      Suppose hypothetical implementer applies IC-8a's
      CONSERVATIVE seed to the immediately-invoked closure
      `f`:
        contracts[0] = ParamContract::CONSERVATIVE;
        // (Owned, Unrestricted, Many, Unknown, MaybeShared,
        // may_share=true)

      Then `f`'s parameter `x` would receive CONSERVATIVE
      contract despite the single visible call site passing
      `42` (an int scalar with no RC concern). Downstream
      consumers (Step 5 emission) would emit Owned ABI for
      `x` (per Access = Owned), expect Many uses (per
      Cardinality = Many), runtime IsShared checks (per
      Uniqueness = MaybeShared) — all unnecessary for an
      immediately-invoked closure with a single scalar
      argument.

      Per Annex E §AIMS §1 ("RC rare, not RC fast"):
      this is a precision regression. The enumerable closure's
      single call site has sufficient evidence to prove tight
      contracts via IC-2 + IC-3; the CONSERVATIVE seed
      over-approximates and emits unnecessary code. The
      carve-out classification is therefore load-bearing for
      AIMS precision; conflating enumerable and non-enumerable
      cases is a precision regression even though both produce
      sound contracts.

      Negative-direction witness — applying OPTIMISTIC seed to
      non-enumerable function rejected:

      Take a public-API function:
        pub @f(x: int) -> int = x + 1;

      Suppose hypothetical implementer applies IC-2's
      OPTIMISTIC seed to the public-API function `f`:
        contracts[0] = ParamContract::OPTIMISTIC;
        // (Borrowed, Dead, Absent, BlockLocal, Unique,
        // may_share=false)

      Then `f`'s parameter `x` would receive OPTIMISTIC
      contract despite non-enumerable external callers.
      Without any call sites visible to the compiler, the
      SCC fixpoint would converge to OPTIMISTIC (the seed)
      — no joins applied. Downstream consumers (Step 5
      emission) would emit Borrowed ABI for `x` (per Access =
      Borrowed), assume Absent cardinality (no uses) — both
      WRONG for an externally-called function. External
      callers may pass owned values with multiple uses; the
      contract under-approximates observable demands.

      Per Annex E §AIMS §2 invariant 1 ("contracts and
      realization must agree"), this is a soundness failure:
      external callers passing Owned arguments with Many
      cardinality would mismatch the function's Borrowed +
      Absent contract, leading to RC imbalance (caller incs
      not balanced by callee decs) or incorrect ABI
      (caller-side `move` for Owned, callee-side `&borrow`
      for Borrowed). The IC-8a CONSERVATIVE seed is therefore
      load-bearing for non-enumerable cases; OPTIMISTIC seed
      is unsound.

    Coherence side-conditions for (P1)..(P5):

      - Classification soundness (Preconditions): the
        "address-taken / non-enumerable" classification at
        analysis time MUST be conservative — when in doubt,
        classify as non-enumerable. False negatives (treating
        a non-enumerable function as enumerable) are
        soundness failures; false positives (treating an
        enumerable function as non-enumerable) are precision
        regressions but sound. Per Annex E §AIMS §2
        invariant 5 ("the unified model must stay unified"),
        the classification feeds the lattice-driven analysis
        as a typed pre-pass input on `AimsStateMap` (similar
        to immortal detection per Annex E §AIMS); no separate
        shadow analysis.

      - Lattice property preservation (P2 + P4): the
        CONSERVATIVE seed is the lattice TOP across 5 of 6
        dimensions (uniqueness = MaybeShared 1 below Shared
        per P3 rationale); the IC-3 max-join operator
        preserves TOP under join per L-6 (`a ⊔ TOP = TOP`).
        Per L-1 + L-2 (commutativity + associativity), the
        fold-order across observed call sites is irrelevant —
        the converged contract is determined by the seed +
        the set of observed argument states, not by fold
        order.

      - Carve-out completeness (P5): the address-taken
        classification is binary (enumerable XOR
        non-enumerable); every function in the program
        receives exactly one classification. IC-2's
        OPTIMISTIC seeding and IC-8a's CONSERVATIVE seeding
        are mutually exclusive — no function receives both.
        Per Annex E §AIMS §2 invariant 5, the binary
        classification preserves the unified-model invariant;
        no shadow seeding mechanism bypasses the lattice
        join.

      - SCC fixpoint compatibility (P4): IC-8a's CONSERVATIVE
        seed participates in the SCC fixpoint loop identically
        to IC-2's OPTIMISTIC seed — both seeds feed the same
        IC-3 max-join + may_share OR-monoid operator. Per
        IC-7's convergence bound (proven separately), the
        SCC fixpoint terminates within
        `param_count × 13 + 8 + 6 + 4` iterations regardless
        of the seed choice; the seed determines the starting
        point, not the convergence behavior.

      - Per-dimension MaybeShared rationale (P3): the
        uniqueness dimension deviation from lattice TOP is
        explicit in the spec rule line. The choice is
        SOUNDNESS-PRESERVING (MaybeShared is sound for all
        non-enumerable cases per DP-4 runtime check) and
        PRECISION-PRESERVING (avoids the unconditional copy
        forced by Shared per DP-9 `Shared ⟹ StaticShared`).
        No other dimension has a similar lattice-TOP
        deviation — IC-8a's seed is the maximally-precise
        sound seed per dim.

    Convergence side-condition (cross-cite to IC-7):

      IC-7 (proven separately) bounds the SCC fixpoint
      iteration at `param_count × 13 + 8 + 6 + 4` per spec
      formula. IC-8a's CONSERVATIVE seed does NOT extend the
      iteration bound — the seed is the lattice TOP per dim
      (5 of 6 exact TOP; uniqueness 1 below TOP), so the
      maximum height advance per parameter is at most 1
      (uniqueness: MaybeShared → Shared) regardless of how
      many observed call sites the SCC contains.

      For purely non-enumerable functions (zero observed call
      sites), the SCC fixpoint terminates in 1 iteration
      (the acknowledgment iteration confirming no change per
      IC-7's `saturating_add(1)` accommodation). The
      CONSERVATIVE seed is preserved unchanged through the
      fixpoint.

      For mixed enumerable / non-enumerable SCCs (where some
      functions have visible call sites and others don't),
      the IC-7 bound covers the cumulative height advance
      across all functions in the SCC; IC-8a's seeded
      functions contribute at most 1 height advance per
      parameter (uniqueness), while IC-2's seeded functions
      contribute up to `13` height advances per parameter
      (spec) / `17` (shipped per IC-7's spec-vs-shipped
      carve-out). The IC-7 bound formula accommodates both
      seed types via the per-parameter height term.

